Z||000000||AusFiero||05-12-2001||04:21 AM||||I was just wondering, after reading a few convertible posts, t-top posts and the general quest for the wind in your hair. <BR>2 ideas here, both feasible.<P>1. Relocate the computer and wiring harness in a Fiero and install an electric wind down rear window. (considering this for my t-topped car. <P>2. A convertible top that is actually a 3 or 4 piece hard top that can be stored in the car. Could look like a standard coupe till the top goes AWOL. Would take up all of the availale storage space but I figure you don't buy a convertible Fiero to take the family away in.<P>Has anybody thrown these ideas around before ?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero.gif"> <BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||5
