Z||000011||DaRkLoRD||05-12-2001||06:22 PM||||Doesn't the vacuum created by the air flowing over the roof and down onto the decklid help draw hot air out of the engine compartment? adding a window there that could roll down would not only reduce this effect, but at low speeds, the noise would be insane, and there could be harmful vapors flowing into the cabin.. the Del Sol doesn't have the engine in the back, so it's not a problem for them..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
Z||000012||Patrick's Dad||05-12-2001||07:08 PM||||Actually, this was one of my weird ideas a couple of years ago. I'm not claiming credit for it, but I have put some thought to it.<P>My thought was to brace the car, then take the center section (a la targa), the resultant "hoop," and that glass out as three sections. I also liked the Del Sol idea, so I considered a keyholed strikeplate on the body with a pin on the B-pillar that would lock it in place. This all seemed like an awful lot of work, especially when I saw the convertibles here, so I shelved the idea, at least permanently, myself.<P>I also continue to consider the 4wd Fiero, which now makes more sense as the Jalapeno has been released.||||reg||1
